---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import InfoLink from '../../components/InfoLink.astro';
import type { FaqItem } from '../../data/faq';
import { product } from '../../data/product';
import { sources } from '../../data/sources';

const faqs: readonly FaqItem[] = [
	{
		question: 'Can you learn AI automation without paying for AI Agency Engine?',
		answer:
			'Yes. Make Academy, Zapier Academy, and n8n’s learning paths publish free courses. Those courses teach the tools. They do not include the advertised AI Agency Engine class.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Is the $47 class a Make, Zapier, or n8n course?',
		answer:
			'The public pages do not describe it that way. They show Murage, a local-business demo, and a live class. Confirm the tools on the checkout. Do not assume a tool subscription is included.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Who should skip the paid class?',
		answer:
			'Someone who wants deep practice in one automation product, and who will design their own service offer, can start with that product’s official academy.',
	},
];

const rows = [
	{
		need: 'Learn a specific automation tool',
		training: 'Not what the public class pages itemize.',
		solo: 'Make, Zapier, and n8n each publish their own courses.',
	},
	{
		need: 'See a service pitch for a local business',
		training: 'The free videos show a website becoming a demo and a sales email.',
		solo: 'You would design that offer yourself after you can build the workflow.',
	},
	{
		need: 'A dated live walkthrough',
		training: `Advertised for ${product.schedule.masterclass}, weekdays at ${product.schedule.masterclassTime}.`,
		solo: 'The academies describe self-paced lessons, not this class schedule.',
	},
	{
		need: 'A published syllabus',
		training: 'The five class days are dated. The lesson list is not published.',
		solo: 'Each academy lists its own courses and paths on its site.',
	},
];
---

<GuidePage
	title="AI Agency Engine vs Learning AI Automation Yourself"
	description="AI Agency Engine vs learning AI automation yourself: the advertised live class beside the official Make, Zapier, and n8n courses."
	label="Self-study"
	h1="AI Agency Engine vs Learning AI Automation Yourself"
	crumb="Vs self-study"
	path="/ai-agency-engine-vs-learning-ai-automation-yourself/"
	related={[
		'/ai-agency-engine-alternatives/',
		'/how-to-start-an-ai-agency/',
		'/ai-agency-engine-masterclass/',
	]}
	faqs={faqs}
	cta="Explore AI Agency Engine"
	closingTitle="Match the spend to the skill you actually want"
	closingText="If you want the seller’s local-business walkthrough, review the $47 offer and the November 2026 dates. If you want a tool, start with that tool’s official academy."
>
	<p class="lede" slot="lede">
		Learning AI automation yourself and buying AI Agency Engine solve different problems. The academies teach you to build workflows. The advertised class is aimed at turning a local business problem into a demonstration and an offer. Pay for the path that matches the gap you have.
	</p>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>What official self-study actually covers</h2>
			<div class="feature-grid">
				<article class="feature-card">
					<Icon name="workflow" />
					<h3>Make Academy</h3>
					<p>
						<InfoLink href={sources.makeAcademy}>Make Academy</InfoLink> describes free, self-paced courses, including scenarios and AI agents. Its FAQ says no prior experience is required for the fundamentals.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="feature-card">
					<Icon name="training" />
					<h3>Zapier Academy</h3>
					<p>
						<InfoLink href={sources.zapierAcademy}>Zapier Academy</InfoLink> describes free courses, from a first Zap to AI workflows. A free Zapier account saves progress. Courses are self-paced.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="feature-card">
					<Icon name="layers" />
					<h3>n8n Academy</h3>
					<p>
						<InfoLink href={sources.n8nLearning}>n8n’s docs</InfoLink> point to <InfoLink href={sources.n8nAcademy}>n8n Academy</InfoLink> for hands-on courses, quizzes, and certificates. Most practice exercises do not need outside accounts.
					</p>
				</article>
			</div>
			<p class="measure">
				Free courses can still sit on top of a paid software plan. This page does not quote those plan prices. Read each product’s current pricing before you build a client offer on it.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section band">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>A tool skill is not yet a service</h2>
			<p class="measure">
				You can finish a course and still have no one to call. A local business pays for a result it understands: a missed inquiry gets a draft reply, an estimate gets a follow-up, a staff member gets a morning brief. Someone has to choose that problem, show a safe demo, name the limits, and deliver it. The academies do not do that selling for you.
			</p>
			<p class="measure">
				AI Agency Engine’s public pages aim at that second job. The free videos follow a dentist website into a demo and an email. Murage proposes a team and waits for approval. The paid piece is the live class at {product.advertisedEntryPrice.label}, separate from the free registration. The pages do not publish a day-by-day syllabus, so do not treat the class as a hidden Make or n8n curriculum.
			</p>
			<div class="table-wrap">
				<table class="offer-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">You need</th>
							<th scope="col">Advertised class</th>
							<th scope="col">Official tool courses</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{
							rows.map((row) => (
								<tr>
									<th scope="row">{row.need}</th>
									<td data-label="Advertised class">{row.training}</td>
									<td data-label="Official tool courses">{row.solo}</td>
								</tr>
							))
						}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>How to choose</h2>
			<ul class="note-list">
				<li>If you cannot yet build a simple workflow, start with the academy for the tool you expect to use.</li>
				<li>If you can build, but you cannot explain an offer to a local owner, the class preview is the more direct look.</li>
				<li>If you need the lesson list and refund rule before spending {product.advertisedEntryPrice.label}, read them on the checkout. <a href="/ai-agency-engine-pricing/">The pricing guide</a> separates that price from the free preview.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="measure">
				<a href="/how-to-start-an-ai-agency/">How to start an AI agency</a> is the practical sequence either path still has to follow.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</GuidePage>
